te-Anne-des-Pins","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Paroisse_Ste-Anne-des-Pins_%281%29.jpg/1280px-Paroisse_Ste-Anne-des-Pins_%281%29.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Paroisse_Ste-Anne-des-Pins_%281%29.jpg/500px-Paroisse_Ste-Anne-des-Pins_%281%29.jpg","w":1200,"h":540,"author":"Silver Dovelet","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Paroisse_Ste-Anne-des-Pins_(1).jpg"}},{"id":"greater_sudbury_ecole_saint_louis_de_gonzague","areaId":"greater_sudbury","name":"École Saint-Louis-de-Gonzague","category":"landmark","tags":["history","photo"],"location":{"lat":46.49684,"lng":-80.99755},"visitMinutes":45,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"greater_sudbury_ecole_saint_louis_de_gonzague","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":0,"commonsNearby":3,"wikiPageviews":34,"wikidataSitelinks":2,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-21"},"hashtags":["ecolesaintlouisdegonzague","greatersudbury"],"bestLight":"morning","summary":"École Saint-Louis de Gonzague is a historic building and former school in the Uptown neighbourhood of Sudbury, Ontario, Canada. Constructed in 1915, it is the oldest school building still standing in Sudbury.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"École Saint-Louis-de-Gonzague (Sudbury)","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Ecole_Saint_Louis_de_Gonzague.jpg/1280px-Ecole_Saint_Louis_de_Gonzague.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Ecole_Saint_Louis_de_Gonzague.jpg/500px-Ecole_Saint_Louis_de_Gonzague.jpg","w":1200,"h":583,"author":"Acoteleg","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ecole_Saint_Louis_de_Gonzague.jpg"}}],"sources":["Wikidata (CC0)","Wikimedia Commons (counts; photos credited per file)","Wikipedia (pageviews; summaries CC BY-SA 4.0)","Wi